Z||000011||Bob Englert||04-17-2001||10:27 PM||||Terry:<P>When we got my daughter's 87 coupe the left rear toe link was completely worn out at the cradle connection.  The car drove as if it had 4 wheel steer (very badly) and had a great deal of play.  Ed Parks replaced it with a good used one when he installed the remanufactured motor.  The car had about 160K when it was replaced.<P>I do know from experience that they can wear out.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
